<p>Text inserted in the top margin of each page of a document is called 
 a header, and text inserted in the bottom margin is called a footer. Besides 
 date, page number, and file name, text of up to 16 double-byte or 32 single-byte 
 characters can be inserted into these areas.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>If you print a document using the Reduce/Enlarge 
 function, the header and footer will also be reduced or enlarged.</p></li>
<li><p>A header and footer will be printed on every page. 
 For example, if you print several document pages on a sheet of paper (Layout), 
 a header and footer will appear on every page.</p></li>
<li><p>If you want to print a header and footer on every 
 sheet but not every page, clear the <span class="Term-Soft">Per Original 
 Page</span> check box. </p></li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box after 
 creating a document in an application.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Effects</span> 
 menu on the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the<span class="Term-Soft"> Header/Footer</span> 
 check box.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the items that you want to print on header 
 and footer, <span class="Term-Soft">Date and Time</span>, <span class="Term-Soft">Page 
 Number</span>, and <span class="Term-Soft">Text</span>.</p></li>
<li><p>To edit the header and footer items, click <span class="Term-Soft">Details...</span> to open the <span class="Term-Soft">Edit 
 Header/Footer</span> dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Date and Time</span> 
 group, select a position and a format for printing date and time.</p></li>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Page Number</span> 
 group, select a position and a format for printing page number.</p></li>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Text</span> group, 
 select a position and a format for printing text. If you select <span class="Term-Soft">User Text</span> in the <span class="Term-Soft">Format:</span> 
 list, enter the text for header/footer in the <span class="Term-Soft">Text:</span> 
 box using up to 32 single-byte or 16 double-byte characters.</p></li>
<li><p>Specify a font and font size in <span class="Term-Soft">Font:</span> 
 and <span class="Term-Soft">Size:</span>.</p></li>
<li><p>To print header and footer per page of document, 
 select the <span class="Term-Soft">Per Original Page</span> check box.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">OK</span> to close 
 the dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>After making any other necessary settings, click 
 <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the printing preferences dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Start printing.</p></li>
</ol>
